body:
It seems like in the cases of failure, 

https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/blob/c37330647fefd5993f568ec5a48de84707bfbc8e/independent-projects/resteasy-reactive/client/runtime/src/main/java/org/jboss/resteasy/reactive/client/impl/MultiInvoker.java#L161

is getting called **before** 

https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/blob/c37330647fefd5993f568ec5a48de84707bfbc8e/independent-projects/resteasy-reactive/client/runtime/src/main/java/org/jboss/resteasy/reactive/client/impl/MultiInvoker.java#L170

The thing is that I don't think we even need to have 

```
        connection.closeHandler(v -> {
            multiRequest.emitter.complete();
        });
```

as 

```
        vertxClientResponse.endHandler(v -> {
            multiRequest.emitter.complete();
        });
```

will always be called anyway (and it does seem to always be called **after** the emitting is done).

WDYT @FroMage ?
